    "crystal_structure": "PA-6: monoclinic α-form (hydrogen-bonded sheets), unit cell a:b:c = 0.956:0.801:1.724 nm. PA-6,6: triclinic α and β forms, plus a pseudohexagonal γ form at high temperature.",
    "chain_flexibility_notes": "Regular amide-hydrogen-bonding pattern along the backbone gives nylon 6,6 good mechanical strength, rigidity, and heat/chemical resistance.",
    "tg_relation_notes": "Amide groups hydrogen-bond with absorbed water, which plasticizes the chain: PA-6 Tg falls from ~50-75 °C dry to 3-20 °C at 50% RH and -22 to -32 °C at saturation; PA-6,6 falls from ~56-70 °C dry to -15 °C at saturation.",
